  "interpretation": [
    "RDMA benefits a training step only when significant collectives cross nodes and communication is on the critical path.",
    "The collective microbenchmark proves transport capacity; the matched SFT A/B measures application-level impact.",
    "The 144.81x and 27.09x microbenchmark ratios must not be presented as end-to-end SFT speedups.",
    "The negative control prevents the false conclusion that merely attaching an RDMA device makes every distributed workload faster."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "The SFT runs contain 20 optimizer steps and exclude the first five; they are a throughput experiment, not a convergence study.",
    "The dataset is synthetic and max length is 512, so the exact percentage should not be generalized to other sequence lengths, routing distributions or hardware.",
    "This is LoRA rather than full-parameter training; full-parameter DP, FSDP and ZeRO communication volumes differ.",
    "The third RDMA All-to-All microbenchmark repetition was much slower than the first two, so the report uses three-run medians and exposes the raw variance.",
    "Loss trajectories are comparable but not bitwise identical because distributed floating-point reduction order is nondeterministic; this benchmark does not compare model quality."
  ]
